# KIRAKITAH Development Guidelines

## Architecture

- **Frontend first** — build and publish the user-facing experience before backend work.
- **No backend unless requested** — do not add APIs, databases, CMS, or server integrations unless explicitly instructed.
- **Vercel** is the deployment target; keep the project compatible with Vercel conventions.

## Code quality

- **Mobile-first** — design and implement for small screens first, then scale up.
- **Reusable components** — prefer composable, shared UI over one-off implementations.
- **Accessibility** — use semantic HTML, keyboard support, and sufficient contrast.
- **Performance** — optimize images, avoid unnecessary dependencies, and keep bundles lean.
- **TypeScript** — use TypeScript when the project stack supports it.

## Safety

- **Never commit secrets** — no API keys, tokens, passwords, or `.env.local` files.
- **Inspect before modifying** — read existing code before changing it; do not replace functionality without understanding it.
- **Minimal scope** — avoid large architectural changes or unnecessary dependencies without explicit instruction.
- **Preserve existing work** — do not delete or overwrite established patterns without approval.

## Future integration

Keep eventual backend integration in mind (data shapes, env var patterns) without implementing backend functionality prematurely.
